<article class="env-lemma" id="089C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/089C">Lemma <span data-tag="089C">67.30.10</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : Y \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module with scheme theoretic support $Z \subset X$. If $f$ is flat, then $f^{-1}(Z)$ is the scheme theoretic support of $f^*\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using the characterization of the scheme theoretic support as given in Lemma <a href="/tag/07U0" data-tag="07U0">67.15.3</a> and using the characterization of flat morphisms in terms of étale coverings in Lemma <a href="/tag/03MM" data-tag="03MM">67.30.5</a> we reduce to the case of schemes which is Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/07T9" data-tag="07T9">29.26.14</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>